# Daily encrypted state.db dump → your fork.
#
# Replace REPO_PATH with the absolute path to your hermes-agent-workflow
# clone, then `crontab -e` and paste the line below (uncommented).
#
# What this does: at 03:33 local time, takes an atomic sqlite snapshot
# of ~/.hermes/state.db, dumps the data tables to plaintext SQL,
# git-crypt encrypts the result via the `hermes-data/**` rule in
# .gitattributes, commits + pushes to your fork. ~50KB-1MB encrypted
# churn per day on a steady chat day.
#
# OFF BY DEFAULT. Opt in only after:
#   1. You've initialized git-crypt in your fork.
#   2. You've confirmed `git push` from cron works (SSH agent forwarding
#      or a deploy key — cron jobs don't get an interactive prompt).
#   3. You're OK with daily encrypted commits to your fork.
#
# REPO_PATH must be absolute. Logs to ~/.hermes/logs/sync-hermes-state.log.

# 33 3 * * * REPO_PATH/scripts/sync-hermes-state.sh >> ~/.hermes/logs/sync-hermes-state.log 2>&1
